# =============================================================================
# Build-context hygiene for the REPOSITORY-ROOT Docker context.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: backend/Dockerfile.prod is built with the context set to
# the repository root (Render: Dockerfile Path backend/Dockerfile.prod, Context .;
# docker-compose.prod.yml: context: ..). Docker only honours a .dockerignore that
# sits at the CONTEXT root — i.e. this file, not backend/.dockerignore.
#
# It keeps the upload small and guarantees that no configuration or secret ever
# enters the image (nothing in the Dockerfile copies them anyway).
# =============================================================================

# ---- VCS / CI metadata (never needed inside the image) ----------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github

# ---- Configuration + secrets: MUST NOT enter the build context --------------
.env
.env.*
backend/env.txt
deploy/env/*.env.prod
deploy/.env

# ---- Dependencies + build outputs (rebuilt inside the image) ---------------
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/coverage
**/.turbo
**/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# ---- Logs, caches, local artifacts ----------------------------------------
**/*.log
**/*.err
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc